  "title": "Concrescence is cumulative, not additive",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "e04c5c52-f431-4251-884c-6cd9da444a4d",
      "text": "In each act of becoming the past is not destroyed but taken up in a new occasion that transcends and includes it, so concrescence is cumulative and not additive. For this reason Segall reads Whitehead as an emergentist rather than a constitutive panpsychist.",
